# Grasp an object from the table: find it in the views, get grasps for its points (GraspGenX) and
# rank them, then for the best reachable ones: move to the pre-grasp pose (pick.pregrasp_m back
# along
# the approach), move in along it, close, check the fingers' opening against the object, lift
# (pick.lift_m) and check the fingers still hold it.

# What to pick, as SAM 3.1 reads it, e.g. "red cube".
string prompt

# Instances scoring below this are left out; 0 uses the configured threshold (perception.min_score).
float32 min_score

# Which grasps: "top" (approaches within grasp.top_max_angle_deg of straight down), "side" (flatter
# ones: from the side or diagonally from above), or "auto" (empty: the same): top grasps first, the
# side grasps when no top grasp is reachable (e.g. under a shelf).
string approach
---
bool success
string message

# The grasp that was executed, in the planning frame; valid only when success is true.
piper_msgs/Grasp grasp

# Finger opening after closing, in metres; valid only when success is true.
float64 finger_width_m

# On a failure: the arm is still down at the table or the object; back off before anything else.
bool arm_stuck
---
# "segmenting", "looking_closer", "planning_grasps", "moving_above", "descending", "closing",
# "lifting"
# ("descending" is the move in along the approach, also for a side grasp)
string phase
